{
    "img": "icons/magic/death/skull-energy-light-white.webp",
    "name": "Effect: Severance",
    "system": {
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>You have stopped carrying your power and become it. For <strong>10 rounds</strong>:</p><ul><li>Your spirit weapon's Strikes deal an additional <strong>4d6 spirit</strong> damage.</li><li>You are <strong>immune to fear and death effects</strong>, and to the <strong>frightened</strong> and <strong>doomed</strong> conditions.</li><li><strong>Reiatsu stops mattering.</strong> Your Release Technique and every kid&#333; you know cost <strong>nothing</strong> and have <strong>no frequency limit</strong>.</li><li>You gain your Spirit's <strong>Full Release</strong> ability and its 20-foot pressure emanation, without spending your daily Full Release and without the fatigue.</li><li>Your Speed increases by <strong>20 feet</strong>, and Flash Step's frequency becomes <strong>twice per round</strong>.</li></ul><hr /><p><strong>Waning.</strong> Your Severing Art is strongest the instant you enter Severance and decays every round: <strong>20d6</strong> in the first round, 18d6 in the second, and so on down to <strong>8d6</strong> in the seventh. After the seventh round it <strong>cannot be used at all</strong>.</p><p><em>The longer you survive, the more this state has given you, and the less your ending is worth. There is no dominant line, which is what makes it a decision instead of a script.</em></p>"
        },
